    {
      "name": "medusa.attach_aplus_images",
      "description": "Store Amazon A+ Content images on the PRODUCT (by product_id or sku) so a human can download them for Seller Central; kept apart from the product's image gallery. Never publishes and never deletes. images: [{module, locale?, path | url | data_base64}]. Each image names its A+ module and must be at least that module's size at exactly its ratio — STANDARD_HEADER_IMAGE_TEXT 970x600, STANDARD_IMAGE_TEXT_OVERLAY 970x300, STANDARD_THREE_IMAGE_TEXT 300x300, STANDARD_FOUR_IMAGE_TEXT 220x200, STANDARD_COMPARISON_TABLE 150x300 — png/jpeg within 2 MB; crop before sending. Give locale (BCP-47, e.g. es-ES) when text is drawn into the image; omit it when there is none. Returns one report per image (included, reason: duplicate | rejected, findings); a refused image's findings name the target size.",
